From: MacFinals
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: leave the menu bar/Dock options alone while inactive (C18 fix)

Rasmus (2026-11-24): after Cmd-Tab away from THE FINALS the game took the mouse and keyboard
back; it stopped only after switching to an app with a window on the game's screen. Captured
on macfinals-139 (+macfinals_ui and the macOS system log, session 07:11): after each of six
switches to LibreWolf (on another display) the game went
  SETFRONT LibreWolf -> game PRESENTATIONMODE AllHidden->Normal (+80 ms)
  -> WindowServer SetMenuBars: game made the front process (+20 ms) -> AllHidden again.
No click and no driver activation request was involved. The Steam Helper switch (window on
the game's screen) made the same call without the steal; a later switch with the options
already Normal made none and did not steal.

The cause is updateCoveringPresentation (REC-45 borderless-game menu bar hiding, from
wine-winemac-activation.patch): on deactivation it counted no covering window and called
setPresentationOptions from the background to show the menu bar again. macOS applies an
app's presentation options only while it is frontmost - the Dock switched its UI mode back
to normal on its own at the SETFRONT, 90 ms before our call - so that call bought nothing
and made WindowServer re-front the app. Now the options are not touched while the app is
inactive; applicationDidBecomeActive: (updateFullscreenWindows) brings them up to date.
WINEDEBUG=+macfinals_ui traces each change.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -2398,7 +2398,17 @@
             keep = value && *value == '1';
         }
         if (keep) return;
-        if ([NSApp isActive])
+        /* C18: macOS applies an app's presentation options only while it is frontmost (the
+           Dock drops back to normal by itself when another app comes forward).  Changing
+           them from the background made WindowServer bring this app to the front again
+           (SetMenuBars) whenever the new app had no window on the game's screen: the game
+           took the mouse and keyboard back 20-30 ms after each Cmd-Tab (2026-11-24).  So
+           they are left as they are while inactive and brought up to date on activation. */
+        if (![NSApp isActive])
+        {
+            if (hidden) UI_LOG(@"menu bar/Dock options left hidden while inactive (C18)\n");
+            return;
+        }
         {
             for (NSNumber* windowNumber in [NSWindow windowNumbersWithOptions:0])
             {
@@ -2418,11 +2428,13 @@
             hidden = TRUE;
             options &= ~(NSApplicationPresentationAutoHideDock | NSApplicationPresentationAutoHideMenuBar);
             [NSApp setPresentationOptions:options | ours];
+            UI_LOG(@"menu bar/Dock hidden over a covering window\n");
         }
         else if (!covering && hidden)
         {
             hidden = FALSE;
             [NSApp setPresentationOptions:options & ~ours];
+            UI_LOG(@"menu bar/Dock shown again (no covering window)\n");
         }
     }
 
